# Skip-list for tests/t-zzz-docs.sh — a wiki ```scheme block is skipped
# when its text contains one of these fixed patterns. Every entry needs a
# reason: these blocks are intentional (schematic or pending a feature),
# not rot. Keep this list short — a skip here is an example that never
# gets executed.
THUNK                    # bind-flags.md/binds.md: placeholder, not a real thunk
(MOD ... KEY)            # binds.md: syntax description, not a call
recalculate-fn           # custom-layouts.md: schematic callback names
hl-permission-add!      # permissions.md: config-load-only (startup rules); the
                        # doc test runs mid-session, where it is correctly rejected
hl-clear-crashed-lockscreen!  # scheme-utilities.md: errors when the session is
                        # not locked — which is always true in the harness;
                        # the refusal IS the documented behavior
hl-load (string-append  # core.md / scheme-utilities.md: loading a file the
                        # harness does not have. hl-load REPORTS rather than
                        # raising — that is the documented behaviour and the
                        # reason it exists — so the block answers #f and passes
                        # on its own; what it leaves behind is the log line, and
                        # t-zzzz-exit counts those. The alternative is an
                        # example that only runs if you happen to have the file,
                        # which is worse documentation than a skip.
